<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex raises domestic natural gas prices.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex raises domestic natural gas prices.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said Tuesday it raised domestic natural gas prices for April by seven percent to $1.72 per million British thermal units (mmBtu).</p>
<p>April prices rose from $1.61 per mmBtu in March after dropping from near-record winter levels, Pemex said in a statement. Pemex's average natural gas price in 1996 was $2.21 per mmBtu.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
